  "difficulty_reason": "After ordinary infinite Ramsey is allowed, the substantive problem is still to design a hierarchical coefficient-separated copy and prove that exactly the same finite family of patterns is unavoidable in every ordinal copy. The proof must coordinate equal coordinates along shared prefixes, prohibit equality across levels, and preserve full residual ordinal type while realizing an arbitrary pattern. This is a nonroutine canonicalization and matching extremal construction, rather than a direct Ramsey-theorem application.",
